```
id: SPL-016
name: Remote logon fan-out across many hosts
description: One account performs network or remote-interactive logons to many distinct hosts.
platform: Splunk
mitre_tactic: Lateral Movement
mitre_technique: T1021 Remote Services
severity: Medium
data_source: index=wineventlog (Security)
false_positives: Patching, monitoring and helpdesk accounts; jump hosts.
tuning: Exclude management accounts via lookup; limit to logon type 10 for lower noise.
test_method: Use a lab account to open RDP sessions to several hosts.
owner: <OWNER>
status: Draft
last_review: 2026-11-19
```
index=wineventlog sourcetype="WinEventLog:Security" EventCode=4624 Logon_Type IN (3,10) earliest=-1h
| where NOT match(user,"\$$") AND user!="ANONYMOUS LOGON"
| stats dc(host) AS hosts values(host) AS host_list values(src) AS sources min(_time) AS first_seen max(_time) AS last_seen BY user
| where hosts>=5
| convert ctime(first_seen) ctime(last_seen)
| sort - hosts
